## Third-party data

**DB-IP City Lite** — IP-to-city database, used for the Instagram connector's map to place login
IP addresses approximately. Licensed **CC BY 4.0**: <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>
Attribution: **IP Geolocation by DB-IP** — <https://db-ip.com>

The database files are NOT distributed in this repository (~40 MB, republished monthly).
`web/scripts/fetch-geo-db.mjs` downloads them into `web/public/geo/`. They are optional: without
them the map draws its declared layer — the real GPS points from the export — and reports the
inferred layer as unavailable.

⚠ It is deliberately **not GeoLite2**. MaxMind's database adds an End User Licence Agreement on top
of CC BY-SA 4.0 — an account to download, a tracking pixel on redistribution, and terms revisable by
one party — which a project of this kind has no way to accept on its users' behalf.
